        allow_population_by_field_name = True", "replace": "    model_config = ConfigDict(populate_by_name=True)", "explanation": "Replace the deprecated class Config with model_config = ConfigDict(...). allow_population_by_field_name is renamed to populate_by_name in v2. The aliases were moved to Field() in the previous edit."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/webhook.py:19:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return GitHubPush.parse_obj(payload)", "replace": "    return GitHubPush.model_validate(payload)", "explanation": "parse_obj is deprecated in Pydantic v2 and is replaced by model_validate, which keeps the same behavior."}], "notes": "Four edits, no overlaps. The first edit adds ConfigDict and Field to the import, and BaseModel stays because GitHubPush still uses it. The v1 `fields` config option was removed in v2, so the aliases are now declared with Field(alias=...) on head_commit_id and repo_name. populate_by_name=True preserves the v1 allow_population_by_field_name behavior, so construction by field name still works. The deprecated parse_obj call is replaced with model_validate. No migration documentation was retrieved, so the edits rely on the v2 API as stated in the findings and were not checked against docs. I did not run the code or tests."}
